WEBVTT

00:01.760 --> 00:04.200
Everywhere you look, there's guys everywhere.

00:04.300 --> 00:06.000
It's such a prosaic life.

00:06.130 --> 00:10.540
At times, we comfort our students with a smile and kindness to cheer them up.

00:10.710 --> 00:13.070
We are false idols who make them stronger for each event.

00:13.210 --> 00:15.510
That's what a princess does.

00:15.680 --> 00:17.010
I don't like this!

00:17.150 --> 00:19.210
Let's get to work!

00:20.320 --> 00:26.950
<i>After I met you, you shed</i> <i>some light onto my heart.</i>

00:27.090 --> 00:33.690
<i>I spent my days doing the</i> <i>same things all the time.</i>

00:34.600 --> 00:39.660
<i>I know what I want to</i> <i>say to you every time.</i>

00:39.800 --> 00:46.370
<i>I always have them</i> <i>hidden inside my heart.</i>

00:47.380 --> 00:52.080
<i>I know it's an important feeling...</i>

00:52.280 --> 00:57.740
<i>...and I'm keeping it warm</i> <i>to give it to you someday.</i>

01:00.060 --> 01:05.720
<i>Sound of the bells</i>
<i>I hear from far away...</i>

01:05.830 --> 01:12.630
<i>...makes my heart beat faster and</i> <i>cuts through the sky like the wind.</i>

01:12.770 --> 01:19.440
<i>After I met you, you shed</i> <i>some light onto my heart.</i>

01:19.540 --> 01:25.240
<i>I spent my days doing the</i> <i>same things all the time.</i>

01:25.450 --> 01:32.120
<i>And when it's time to tell you</i> <i>the things I've been wanting to say...</i>

01:32.250 --> 01:37.920
<i>You're my sunshine, an eternal smile!</i>

01:38.230 --> 01:48.230
<i>Our prologue, to this exciting story...</i>

01:50.540 --> 01:56.000
<i>Secret of the Sakamoto Family</i>

02:06.790 --> 02:07.850
Amazing!

02:07.960 --> 02:08.950
Who are they?

02:09.060 --> 02:09.850
Pretty!

02:09.960 --> 02:11.520
Are they shooting a drama?

02:11.660 --> 02:13.320
What's wrong, Aki?

02:13.430 --> 02:15.620
It's nothing, I'm fine.

02:15.800 --> 02:18.390
Anyway, just hurry up and pick something, Aki.

02:18.530 --> 02:19.560
I'm hungry!

02:19.670 --> 02:21.400
Sorry about that, I'll make it quick.

02:24.410 --> 02:25.530
Aki!

02:25.710 --> 02:27.010
Take a look!

02:26.340 --> 02:30.070
<i>I'll pick something quick!</i>

02:27.280 --> 02:30.070
Yeah, I feel sorry for him.

02:34.950 --> 02:35.970
Hey Akira!

02:36.080 --> 02:37.420
Where are you going, Akira?

02:37.550 --> 02:38.610
Akira!

02:44.360 --> 02:45.450
Mr. Sakamoto!

02:45.930 --> 02:48.160
Good morning, Mr. Sakamoto!

02:48.360 --> 02:50.660
Good morning...

02:50.800 --> 02:53.670
Doing your job for the student association, Mr. Sakamoto?

02:53.800 --> 02:54.700
That's right.

02:54.840 --> 02:56.860
You people must be busy with your clubs.

02:57.010 --> 03:00.440
We're not as busy as you, Mr. Sakamoto!

03:00.880 --> 03:02.810
Good luck, Mr. Sakamoto!

03:02.940 --> 03:04.610
Thank you very much.

03:28.770 --> 03:30.800
It's over!

03:30.970 --> 03:33.910
This summer's cheering is finally over.

03:34.210 --> 03:35.140
Yeah...

03:35.510 --> 03:36.770
By the way, where's Mikoto?

03:36.880 --> 03:37.350
What?

03:37.850 --> 03:41.040
Kouno! Shihoudani!

03:41.620 --> 03:43.640
I'll see you guys!

03:44.750 --> 03:47.480
He sure looks happy.

03:47.620 --> 03:50.520
We didn't notify President
Arisada yet, that punk!

03:50.660 --> 03:51.490
Hey!

03:52.390 --> 03:53.190
Yo!

03:53.400 --> 03:54.690
Hey Sakamoto!

03:55.300 --> 03:57.490
What's wrong with Yutaka?
Looked like he was in a hurry...

03:57.600 --> 03:59.800
He went straight to his girlfriend.

03:59.940 --> 04:01.560
Our summer job is done, so...

04:01.700 --> 04:04.140
Doing your job for the student association, Mr. Sakamoto?

04:05.070 --> 04:08.340
Yeah, we have to prepare for next semester.

04:08.480 --> 04:10.310
It must be tough for you, Sakamoto.

04:10.410 --> 04:12.070
No, it's really nothing.

04:12.410 --> 04:13.750
Good job, princesses!

04:15.080 --> 04:16.280
I heard!

04:16.380 --> 04:18.820
Five of our clubs went to the prefectural tournament.

04:18.920 --> 04:20.980
Two of those clubs went to the finals!

04:21.160 --> 04:23.350
It seems we got excellent results!

04:23.490 --> 04:27.360
But unfortunately, we couldn't make it to the all Japan tournament.

04:27.630 --> 04:29.000
Well, that's kind of hard...

04:29.360 --> 04:30.890
I knew it. Right?

04:31.000 --> 04:31.560
Yeah.

04:32.100 --> 04:32.970
Of course...

04:33.070 --> 04:35.000
...we're no match for you, president...

04:37.040 --> 04:38.770
That's not true.

04:39.880 --> 04:41.100
I see...

04:41.440 --> 04:43.880
You guys worked really hard.

04:43.980 --> 04:45.070
Thank you!

04:45.210 --> 04:47.050
We don't have many days until the summer ends...

04:47.150 --> 04:50.350
...but try to enjoy the rest of your vacation.

04:50.490 --> 04:52.110
We're saved!

04:52.250 --> 04:55.490
Wearing this makes me feel so hot, but we're finally done.

04:55.690 --> 04:57.420
Then president, I think I'll just...

04:57.660 --> 04:58.520
Mr. Sakamoto!

04:58.660 --> 04:59.590
Yes!

04:59.900 --> 05:02.490
I need you to stay for the briefing session...

05:02.600 --> 05:05.530
...on the scheduling for the upcoming semester.

05:05.800 --> 05:06.930
I see...

05:07.040 --> 05:08.090
Listen!

05:08.200 --> 05:11.970
Mr. Sakamoto is the younger brother of the previous Mr. Sakamoto.

05:12.110 --> 05:16.910
There's no one but you to take my place as president of this school!

05:17.080 --> 05:19.980
But I'm just an ordinary student!

05:20.280 --> 05:21.610
Mr. Sakamoto!

05:21.720 --> 05:22.650
Yes!

05:23.350 --> 05:27.190
I can't see how that man's younger brother is just an ordinary student.

05:27.360 --> 05:31.350
The previous Mr. Sakamoto was so great that even I was no match for him.

05:31.560 --> 05:34.530
He was untouchable...

05:34.800 --> 05:36.090
What are you saying, Arisada!

05:36.460 --> 05:38.900
It's true that Mr. Sakamoto was great.

05:39.000 --> 05:40.830
But so were you!

05:40.200 --> 05:40.830
<i>That's right!</i>

05:40.940 --> 05:42.770
Don't say you were no match for Mr. Sakamoto!

05:43.100 --> 05:45.230
No, I was no match for him...

05:45.410 --> 05:46.400
That's not true!

05:46.510 --> 05:47.530
Be confident!

05:47.640 --> 05:48.630
Arisada!

05:49.110 --> 05:53.450
Well, in any case, I'm counting on you, Mr. Sakamoto!

05:53.580 --> 05:54.680
Yes...

05:57.820 --> 05:59.340
He must've been really great.

06:13.030 --> 06:15.590
Tohru, do you know how to do this?

06:15.740 --> 06:17.140
Let me see.

06:18.970 --> 06:19.910
Nope...

06:20.240 --> 06:22.210
I can't help you with this.

06:22.380 --> 06:24.970
I'm sure Sakamoto knows this stuff.

06:25.910 --> 06:28.780
You know what? Sakamoto did ask us to come to his house!

06:28.950 --> 06:30.820
Let's go visit him so he can help you!

06:31.950 --> 06:34.920
Then I'll check the ones that I think are hard.

06:35.060 --> 06:37.750
Hey, you think we can meet the previous Mr. Sakamoto?

06:37.860 --> 06:38.590
What?

06:38.690 --> 06:39.560
Oh yeah!

06:39.660 --> 06:41.530
The previous Mr. Sakamoto is there too!

06:41.630 --> 06:44.290
Exactly! He said they're all living together!

06:44.700 --> 06:46.530
Let's go and stay over his place!

06:46.740 --> 06:49.470
Then our chances of meeting them will be greater!

06:49.570 --> 06:50.730
You're right!

06:51.270 --> 06:53.670
They said we're off until the new semester, so we've got nothing else to do.

06:53.940 --> 06:56.240
All right, I'll go and call him!

06:56.710 --> 06:58.110
I'm counting on you!

07:04.250 --> 07:05.980
You said it was the north exit, right?

07:06.090 --> 07:09.290
Yeah, and this is the only north exit...

07:09.420 --> 07:10.590
Hey!

07:10.890 --> 07:12.550
This way, you two!

07:12.860 --> 07:15.260
Sorry for making you come and pick us up.

07:15.360 --> 07:18.530
It's okay, my place is just 10 minutes from here by foot.

07:18.670 --> 07:19.530
Well!

07:20.100 --> 07:22.040
Is the great Mr. Sakamoto in today?

07:22.140 --> 07:23.370
What?

07:22.570 --> 07:23.370
<i>Is he or isn't he?</i>

07:23.570 --> 07:25.630
Well, I don't know...

07:25.840 --> 07:27.810
He wasn't there when I left...

07:28.040 --> 07:30.510
What do you want to do? Should we stay for 3 days, 2 nights?

07:30.650 --> 07:33.110
No, we gotta stay longer than that.

07:30.910 --> 07:31.910
<i>Umm...</i>

07:33.250 --> 07:35.480
But I didn't bring that much clothing!

07:35.650 --> 07:39.020
Anyway, I don't want you guys to be surprised when you come to my house.

07:39.320 --> 07:40.580
Surprised?

07:40.720 --> 07:41.490
About what?

07:41.860 --> 07:44.490
Well you know, about my brother and stuff...

07:44.590 --> 07:46.560
Oh, you mean that!

07:47.100 --> 07:48.220
Don't worry about it.

07:48.330 --> 07:51.200
We work as princesses, we're pretty much used to anything.

07:51.330 --> 07:52.930
Then I have nothing to worry about...

07:59.470 --> 08:00.340
This is it.

08:00.640 --> 08:01.470
It's huge.

08:01.580 --> 08:03.910
It's a really nice house.

08:04.010 --> 08:06.070
Wait a minute, is your family super rich?

08:06.180 --> 08:06.580
What?

08:07.150 --> 08:11.510
I heard he's from a very wealthy family!

08:07.780 --> 08:11.510
<i>No! My father's in the architectural business!</i>

08:12.250 --> 08:16.210
Anyway, let's just go inside and drink something cold, it's really hot out here!

08:16.360 --> 08:18.220
I agree!

08:19.730 --> 08:20.960
I'm home!

08:21.100 --> 08:22.720
Excuse us!

08:26.370 --> 08:28.390
Are they your friends, Aki?

08:28.540 --> 08:29.870
Yeah, Kouno and Shihoudani!

08:30.010 --> 08:31.840
Hello, and welcome!

08:32.410 --> 08:33.770
Yes, hello!

08:35.410 --> 08:38.180
I'll go and get you some cold drinks.

08:38.610 --> 08:42.180
Aki, show them to their rooms, okay?

08:42.320 --> 08:43.440
Yeah, okay.

08:44.620 --> 08:48.150
Did you see some flowers right behind her?

08:48.320 --> 08:51.760
Yeah, I saw them too, it was very girly-like...

08:52.130 --> 08:54.600
Your rooms are upstairs, so come with me.

08:54.730 --> 08:55.750
Sakamoto!

08:56.730 --> 08:59.720
She was rather cute, is she your older sister?

08:59.830 --> 09:00.560
No way!

09:00.670 --> 09:02.460
I knew it...

09:00.870 --> 09:02.460
<i>She must be his younger sister!</i>

09:02.600 --> 09:03.630
You're wrong!

09:03.910 --> 09:06.880
She was way too polite to be his younger sister, she must be his older sister!

09:06.980 --> 09:08.140
No way!

09:08.240 --> 09:11.440
She was very bubbly. She must be his younger sister!

09:11.580 --> 09:12.310
Older sister!

09:12.410 --> 09:13.110
Younger sister!

09:13.210 --> 09:14.110
She's his older sister!

09:14.220 --> 09:15.240
She's his younger sister!

09:15.350 --> 09:17.380
Then let's ask him!

09:16.850 --> 09:17.380
<i>Fine!</i>

09:17.890 --> 09:19.320
Which one of us is correct?

09:19.690 --> 09:23.060
No, she's actually my...

09:34.440 --> 09:36.000
I'm his mother!

09:36.200 --> 09:37.100
What?

09:37.470 --> 09:39.530
You're not his older sister?

09:39.810 --> 09:40.900
You're not his younger sister?

09:41.110 --> 09:44.340
Oh, you flatter me!

09:44.510 --> 09:46.210
You two are precious!

09:46.350 --> 09:48.210
I'm making some yakiniku tonight!

09:46.580 --> 09:48.210
<i>Are you two okay?</i>

09:48.620 --> 09:50.210
Kouno, Shihoudani!

09:50.390 --> 09:51.480
Sakamoto...

09:51.590 --> 09:52.610
What is it?

09:52.720 --> 09:55.490
I don't know if I should ask you this but...

09:55.590 --> 09:58.080
Is she your stepmother?

09:59.090 --> 09:59.930
She's my real mother.

10:00.230 --> 10:01.420
What?

10:01.660 --> 10:03.760
Then how old is she?

10:04.030 --> 10:05.630
43 years old.

10:08.070 --> 10:11.270
This is where you're going to be really surprised...

10:11.370 --> 10:12.140
What?

10:12.270 --> 10:14.300
Aki, can I come in?

10:15.180 --> 10:16.370
Aki!

10:17.750 --> 10:18.680
Oh, Fuyuki--

10:18.780 --> 10:20.680
Sorry, I didn't know you had company.

10:21.180 --> 10:22.210
I'll come back later.

10:22.320 --> 10:24.550
No! Don't worry about us.

10:24.650 --> 10:26.590
You can just take care of your business.

10:26.720 --> 10:28.750
Really? Okay, then...

10:32.830 --> 10:35.520
And you see, the relative pronoun is...

10:35.630 --> 10:38.460
Well, you can use either "Which or Whom."

10:38.730 --> 10:40.600
So beautiful...

10:40.700 --> 10:42.690
Yeah, but it must be his younger brother.

10:42.800 --> 10:45.210
No way, we were wrong about his mother.

10:45.340 --> 10:47.210
Don't let the outside appearance fool you.

10:47.340 --> 10:49.000
Then his older brother or father?

10:49.110 --> 10:51.050
But he wouldn't have to teach them, right?

10:51.150 --> 10:52.140
I guess.

10:52.250 --> 10:54.910
Looks much younger than Mr. Sakamoto, too...

10:55.520 --> 10:57.710
Well, sorry for interrupting you guys.

10:57.820 --> 10:58.950
No problem!

10:59.050 --> 11:00.680
We don't mind at all!

11:01.560 --> 11:02.180
And?

11:02.290 --> 11:03.490
Was that your younger brother?

11:03.590 --> 11:05.320
Your older brother or your father?

11:05.460 --> 11:06.480
My younger sister.

11:06.630 --> 11:07.430
Younger sister?

11:07.660 --> 11:08.650
You're lying!

11:08.760 --> 11:11.530
She wasn't anything like your mother!

11:11.670 --> 11:14.660
I told you, you're going to be surprised even more.

11:14.800 --> 11:16.030
We heard you.

11:16.170 --> 11:19.940
But why your mom is so girly, and her daughter is so boyish?

11:21.180 --> 11:21.610
What?

11:24.450 --> 11:26.470
What's wrong you two?

11:27.880 --> 11:30.980
His mother's like that, and his younger sister's like that...

11:32.390 --> 11:35.410
And his legendary older brother, Mr. Sakamoto...

11:36.520 --> 11:38.820
What are you two trying to say?

11:39.290 --> 11:42.920
You said we're still in for a surprise, right?

11:43.060 --> 11:44.190
Yeah...

11:44.330 --> 11:47.600
Could there be any others?

11:49.800 --> 11:51.100
Could it be...

11:52.270 --> 11:55.440
Could it be that your father and your older brother are like that, too?

11:58.280 --> 11:59.680
N-No...

12:00.220 --> 12:01.580
My father's normal.

12:02.020 --> 12:03.510
He's normal!

12:03.890 --> 12:05.680
He's supposed to be normal!

12:08.290 --> 12:11.280
I think he's normal. Probably...

12:11.590 --> 12:13.030
You think?

12:13.160 --> 12:14.820
Probably?

12:16.460 --> 12:17.360
Again?

12:17.470 --> 12:19.160
Who could it be this time?

12:20.770 --> 12:22.130
Akira!

12:22.270 --> 12:24.300
I brought back some food, you want some?

12:25.970 --> 12:28.310
Another gorgeous person...

12:28.440 --> 12:30.500
Male or female?

12:30.880 --> 12:31.610
Which is it?

12:32.350 --> 12:33.140
Nice to meet you!

12:33.280 --> 12:34.910
Just wait a minute!

12:35.020 --> 12:36.040
I'm thinking right now!

12:36.320 --> 12:38.720
Hey, don't forget about what happened before.

12:38.820 --> 12:39.910
I know!

12:40.020 --> 12:41.460
I can't be fooled by their looks.

12:41.590 --> 12:43.460
Maybe it's about time.

12:43.660 --> 12:44.560
What's going on?

12:44.690 --> 12:45.680
It's nothing...

12:45.860 --> 12:48.850
Can't be. It sounded like there might be more.

12:50.700 --> 12:53.330
Fine! I'll say it's the well-known Mr. Sakamoto!

12:53.570 --> 12:55.470
I'll just go and say it's his grandmother!

12:55.600 --> 12:56.400
Wrong!

12:56.570 --> 12:58.840
Sorry, I'm Akira's older sister.

13:00.580 --> 13:03.170
You two are so pretty, yet hilarious!

13:03.410 --> 13:05.210
Eat these with tea if you like.

13:05.310 --> 13:06.940
Make yourselves at home!

13:09.080 --> 13:10.110
Sakamoto...

13:10.220 --> 13:11.080
What is it?

13:11.220 --> 13:14.210
Didn't you say everyone is weird?

13:14.360 --> 13:16.760
You didn't ask about my older sister!

13:16.890 --> 13:17.690
Sakamoto!

13:17.790 --> 13:18.450
Yes!

13:19.290 --> 13:21.530
Let's just make it perfectly clear.

13:21.830 --> 13:22.690
About what?

13:22.800 --> 13:25.630
How many people are in your family?

13:25.770 --> 13:27.100
Six people.

13:28.900 --> 13:31.340
Then all that's left is your father and your older brother!

13:31.470 --> 13:33.370
The next person we meet is going to be the biggest challenge!

13:33.470 --> 13:36.000
What? Why is this becoming a challenge?

13:37.210 --> 13:38.340
He's here!

13:38.450 --> 13:39.540
Nice timing!

13:40.780 --> 13:42.220
Hello.

13:42.380 --> 13:43.720
I heard your friends are here.

13:44.190 --> 13:45.020
What?

13:45.120 --> 13:46.640
Yeah, that's right.

13:52.660 --> 13:54.650
Here's another one with a sparkling entrance...

13:54.800 --> 13:57.430
Is he the father, or is he the older brother?

13:57.530 --> 13:59.760
No, he looks too young to be his father!

13:59.870 --> 14:03.770
If he's the father, then he's immortal just like the mother!

14:04.070 --> 14:07.410
Are they really humans like us?

14:10.710 --> 14:12.610
Nice to meet you, I'm Akira's...

14:12.710 --> 14:13.580
Hold it!

14:15.680 --> 14:19.750
He was in control of the entire school, but he doesn't seem dignified at all.

14:19.890 --> 14:21.380
Or maybe it's like this.

14:21.490 --> 14:25.360
It's his winning smile and friendly attitude that attracted so many people!

14:26.090 --> 14:29.620
I mean, why do they all look so beautiful?

14:29.830 --> 14:32.390
Maybe they're not human after all.

14:32.530 --> 14:33.800
They're not really human?

14:34.240 --> 14:36.100
What's going on, you two?

14:36.240 --> 14:38.260
What were you guys talking about?

14:38.440 --> 14:40.470
Hey you guys!

14:40.710 --> 14:42.230
Are we good now?

14:42.340 --> 14:44.400
Nice to meet you, I'm Akira's father.

14:52.590 --> 14:57.320
They say it all the time, that our family is a bit odd.

14:58.430 --> 15:00.730
I seem to be normal, but...

15:00.830 --> 15:02.190
Hide!

15:02.830 --> 15:04.590
Only a bit odd?

15:04.830 --> 15:06.320
They're really odd...

15:06.670 --> 15:10.000
Hey, I was looking all over for you, Hide!

15:10.140 --> 15:13.370
It's just not fair to have me cook all by myself!

15:13.570 --> 15:15.300
Oh, sorry about that.

15:15.410 --> 15:16.940
This is to show that I'm sorry.

15:17.080 --> 15:19.210
Hide, you...

15:20.250 --> 15:22.270
How do I react to all this?

15:22.380 --> 15:24.880
Are they really past 40?

15:25.020 --> 15:27.820
Is this what goes on all the time, Sakamoto?

15:27.920 --> 15:28.860
Yeah...

15:28.960 --> 15:30.220
Everyday must be hard for you...

15:32.330 --> 15:34.320
Oh, you...

15:39.800 --> 15:41.900
Hide, it's burning up!

15:42.200 --> 15:44.200
Sorry, I totally forgot!

15:45.840 --> 15:50.870
I was kind of excited to see the famous Mr. Sakamoto today.

15:51.010 --> 15:54.380
But your family really surprised us for sure.

15:54.780 --> 15:57.250
That's right, my palms were sweating the whole time!

15:58.550 --> 16:00.920
But wasn't it hard for you?

16:01.060 --> 16:02.890
To be surrounded by family members like them?

16:03.020 --> 16:04.490
Oh wait, you're a member of this family...

16:04.590 --> 16:06.560
...I guess you don't think that way about them.

16:06.930 --> 16:08.760
No, that's not true.

16:08.860 --> 16:09.190
What?

16:10.970 --> 16:12.400
That's not true.

16:12.500 --> 16:16.130
I didn't think my family was weird.

16:16.370 --> 16:19.400
I felt like I was the one who didn't fit in.

16:19.640 --> 16:20.130
What?

16:26.050 --> 16:26.980
Take a look!

16:27.080 --> 16:31.250
If you compare my face with theirs, it looks normal and different from them, right?

16:31.820 --> 16:33.220
That's not true.

16:33.350 --> 16:35.290
You don't have to be nice like that.

16:35.390 --> 16:37.820
I've been told I look different ever since I was a kid.

16:39.190 --> 16:44.760
Even with that, there were times when
I was troubled and I worried a lot.

16:44.930 --> 16:46.800
I don't know if I'm used to it now, but...

16:46.900 --> 16:50.170
I realized that it was wrong for me to think that way about myself.

16:50.340 --> 16:53.400
Nobody says negative things about me, so...

16:54.780 --> 16:57.470
I have to be very confident about myself.

16:57.610 --> 17:00.980
Then I'll have no problem figuring out where I belong...

17:01.120 --> 17:05.050
...or what is really important to me...

17:06.190 --> 17:08.420
Now that I understand it,
I'm much more comfortable.

17:12.060 --> 17:13.220
I got it!

17:13.330 --> 17:16.350
The way you were able to overcome everything and accept them...

17:16.500 --> 17:18.990
...is because you're very quick to understand things!

17:19.100 --> 17:20.400
I see!

17:20.500 --> 17:22.130
Understand?

17:22.270 --> 17:23.800
Anyway...

17:24.040 --> 17:26.800
I'm going to tell you honestly...

17:26.910 --> 17:29.470
I want you to stop calling me Mr. Sakamoto.

17:29.580 --> 17:30.410
What?

17:30.980 --> 17:35.970
When they call me Mr. Sakamoto, it feels like an invisible wall has been created.

17:36.250 --> 17:39.190
It feels like they're talking to me through an invisible wall...

17:39.320 --> 17:43.220
So I'm glad that you guys came over today...

17:43.960 --> 17:48.050
I want to deal with close friends like yourselves in a normal way, at least.

17:48.830 --> 17:49.820
Sakamoto...

17:50.800 --> 17:52.990
Thank you so much for coming today...

17:56.300 --> 17:58.500
We don't care about your older brother.

17:58.610 --> 17:58.940
What?

17:59.470 --> 18:01.470
We're with you, Sakamoto...

18:02.010 --> 18:04.670
We became friends with Akira Sakamoto.

18:05.310 --> 18:06.750
That's right.

18:08.350 --> 18:10.440
Kouno, Shihoudani...

18:10.620 --> 18:15.150
So I'll be like Tohru and simply just call you "Sakamoto".

18:15.590 --> 18:16.520
Wait!

18:16.990 --> 18:19.360
Let's just call him by his first name then!

18:20.190 --> 18:21.860
We call each other by our first names too.

18:22.760 --> 18:24.490
Or would you prefer "Sakamoto"?

18:24.600 --> 18:25.360
What?

18:25.700 --> 18:27.290
No, that's perfectly fine!

18:27.400 --> 18:27.800
Okay!

18:28.200 --> 18:32.200
Then Tohru and I are going to start calling you Akira from now on!

18:32.340 --> 18:35.500
So you call us by our first names too, okay?

18:35.810 --> 18:36.940
Okay.

18:37.280 --> 18:37.940
Got it!

18:38.450 --> 18:40.070
Now let's practice.

18:40.280 --> 18:41.680
My name is Tohru.

18:41.780 --> 18:43.380
My name is Yujirou.

18:43.520 --> 18:44.610
Now say it.

18:45.090 --> 18:47.080
Tohru! Yujirou!

18:50.560 --> 18:52.530
This is kind of embarrassing!

18:52.630 --> 18:54.460
You shouldn't be embarrassed that much...

18:54.530 --> 18:56.330
Well, it's like that in the beginning.

18:56.430 --> 18:57.900
You'll get used to it.

18:58.000 --> 19:00.630
Anyway, we'll just...

18:59.400 --> 19:00.630
<i>Akira!</i>

19:16.320 --> 19:18.010
Could that be...

19:18.390 --> 19:20.910
T-The legendary Mr. Sakamoto?

19:24.790 --> 19:26.190
Akira!

19:27.560 --> 19:28.290
What?

19:32.370 --> 19:33.800
You're so mean, Akira!

19:33.900 --> 19:37.860
Why didn't you tell me you guys were having yakiniku tonight?

19:43.480 --> 19:44.880
What?

19:45.010 --> 19:49.420
Why didn't you tell me about this important dinner, Akira?

19:49.520 --> 19:53.350
I tried sending an email to your cell phone but...

19:59.430 --> 20:02.160
Oh, I see...

20:02.800 --> 20:04.060
I'm sorry, Akira!

20:04.170 --> 20:07.330
You're the only one that really cares about me!

20:07.640 --> 20:10.700
Brother Haru, my friends are here and so...

20:14.280 --> 20:15.140
His older brother...

20:15.240 --> 20:17.710
He's the legendary Mr. Sakamoto?

20:17.880 --> 20:20.250
He's beautiful but...

20:20.610 --> 20:22.210
Yeah, he's really beautiful.

20:22.320 --> 20:24.680
But he's the right age and all.

20:24.820 --> 20:26.550
He looks like a man...

20:27.220 --> 20:28.880
What are you guys talking about?

20:29.020 --> 20:31.120
He was clinging onto Akira.

20:31.230 --> 20:34.680
We can't even sense a bit of charisma or mysteriousness from him...

20:34.860 --> 20:36.490
Listen guys...

20:38.270 --> 20:42.030
I mean, after he showed us bunch of beautiful-looking family members...

20:42.140 --> 20:45.530
They all look good, so he just looks normal.

20:43.940 --> 20:45.530
<i>Listen!</i>

20:46.840 --> 20:47.930
I got it!

20:48.340 --> 20:50.780
He gets good grades and is an all-around athlete.

20:50.880 --> 20:52.570
He's got great personality, very popular among the students...

20:52.680 --> 20:54.110
...and has great leadership skills.

20:55.320 --> 20:56.510
What are you talking about?

20:56.780 --> 21:00.650
Plus he's President Arisada's successor!

21:01.020 --> 21:03.750
People around him are great, so he just doesn't stand out as much.

21:03.890 --> 21:05.950
You're really not normal either!

21:06.090 --> 21:07.690
What? Wait a minute!

21:07.960 --> 21:11.160
No, you look great too!

21:11.270 --> 21:12.560
What? No way!

21:12.670 --> 21:14.360
Don't be so modest.

21:14.470 --> 21:15.630
Everyone thinks you're great!

21:15.770 --> 21:18.210
But I'm nothing compared to my brother Haru...

21:18.310 --> 21:19.740
You're comparing yourself to the wrong guy!

21:19.840 --> 21:22.740
No matter what other people say, you're still good-looking!

21:22.840 --> 21:23.610
Right?

21:24.710 --> 21:26.700
What?

21:31.950 --> 21:34.250
Oh no! I forgot my wallet!

21:41.900 --> 21:49.460
<i>If you're sad and feeling</i> <i>down, then call out to me.</i>

21:49.570 --> 21:57.640
<i>I'll be in the area, so let</i> <i>me know what's bothering you.</i>

21:58.150 --> 22:05.480
<i>If you're all by yourself,</i> <i>then you'll forget how to smile.</i>

22:05.590 --> 22:13.320
<i>A smile is something you</i> <i>share with another person.</i>

22:13.460 --> 22:23.460
<i>Hey, the future you can see</i> <i>from the classroom window...</i>

22:23.700 --> 22:30.300
<i>...is getting larger after</i> <i>taking in the sunlight.</i>

22:30.640 --> 22:32.140
<i>Smile at me!</i>

22:32.280 --> 22:40.020
<i>A smile is what makes you feel energetic!</i>

22:40.120 --> 22:46.120
<i>I want to give some smiles to you...</i>

22:46.260 --> 22:48.290
<i>...right away.</i>

22:48.560 --> 22:58.560
<i>In order for you to lift</i> <i>your head up and start walking.</i>

23:05.110 --> 23:10.050
Next Episode, Chorus
Concert of Sweat and Tears
